# What never gets uploaded to a build.
#
# Without this file Vercel falls back to .gitignore. That fallback happens to
# be correct today, but it is a behaviour rather than a guarantee, and the
# thing it is protecting is server/.env — live SMTP, Google and Graph
# credentials. deploy.md §6.5 records that those exact values were uploaded
# to Vercel's environment store once already. Once is enough.
#
# NOTE: the presence of this file REPLACES the .gitignore fallback entirely,
# so anything that must stay out of a build has to be listed here too.

# Secrets — the reason this file exists.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example

# Rebuilt on the build machine; uploading them is slow and can shadow the
# lockfile's resolution.
node_modules
**/node_modules
web/dist

# Repository and tooling internals.
.git
.claude
.vercel
*.log
.DS_Store

# Docs — deploy.md is an operational runbook naming internal hosts and
# network ranges. It has no business in a deployment bundle.
*.md
!README.md
